{
  "_about": "Design tokens for the resume builder. Roles measured from Rezi (see measured below), values are our own placeholders. replica-brand changes the values, never the names. After any change run: python3 replica/design/build_tokens.py && python3 ~/.claude/skills/replica-design/contrast.py replica/design/tokens.json",
  "_measured": {
    "source": "Rezi app, computed styles on the dashboard and editor at 1440px, 2026-10-05",
    "theme": "dark only by default; light theme exists behind a setting (not measured)",
    "greys": "6 (Tailwind slate 950/900/800/700/600 + gray 100/400/500 for text)",
    "accent": "lavender, black text on it; used for primary buttons, active tabs, links, AI suggestion text",
    "secondary_accent": "teal, for NEW badges, the offer banner and passed checks",
    "status": "red errors, amber warnings, green passes, score gauge red/amber/green",
    "type": "sans UI font; serif resume default; labels 12-14px bold UPPERCASE; body 16/24",
    "space": "4px base: 4, 8, 16, 24 most used; card padding 24",
    "radius": "4, 6, 8, pill",
    "layout": "dashboard sidebar 280; editor icon rail 70; editor left column 308; form card 910; content offset 64",
    "controls": "buttons 40-48 high; inputs sit in a 48px bordered field"
  },
  "_decisions": [
    "Light is the default theme and dark is offered; both are checked here. Rezi's dark navy with a lavender accent is its look, so we don't start from it.",
    "The accent is a neutral graphite placeholder until /replica-brand picks a hue.",
    "Labels are sentence case at 14px/500, not bold uppercase: easier to read and not Rezi's style.",
    "Focus, AI and highlight are functional roles with their own colours so they stay visible whatever accent the brand picks.",
    "paper and ink are the resume page itself: white paper and near-black ink in both themes, because the PDF is printed that way."
  ],
